  "notes": "{済|す}む is an intransitive godan verb meaning 'to be finished' or 'to be settled.'\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {済|す}ませる (transitive, to finish/complete)\n\nKEY PATTERNS:\n- Xが{済|す}む: X is finished\n- V-て{済|す}む: can get by with doing V\n- V-ないで{済|す}む: can manage without doing V\n- それで{済|す}む: that will be enough/sufficient\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {仕事|しごと}が{済|す}んだ: the work is done\n- {用事|ようじ}が{済|す}む: business is finished\n- {食事|しょくじ}が{済|す}む: finished eating\n- {謝|あやま}って{済|す}む{問題|もんだい}ではない: not something an apology can fix\n\nNOTE:\nDon't confuse with {住|す}む (to live, to reside), which has the same reading but different kanji and meaning.",
